* Fri Oct 23 2026 Mikko Tenhunen <mikko.tenhunen@kiinteistomestarit.com> 0.5-1
- Updated the application to version 0.5
- Added a new calendar export page
- Added support for exporting public holidays to an iCalendar ICS file
- Added support for exporting Finnish flag days to an iCalendar ICS file
- Added support for exporting public holidays and flag days into the same ICS file
- Added year selection to the calendar export page
- Added options for selecting which event types are exported
- Added automatic ICS file naming based on the selected year and event types
- Added saving of exported ICS files to the Downloads directory
- Added an option for opening an exported ICS file in a compatible calendar application
- Added unique and repeatable identifiers for exported calendar events
- Added UTF-8 support for exported calendar event names and descriptions
- Added all-day DTSTART and DTEND values to exported events
- Added CalendarExporter C++ backend for creating calendar files
- Added HolidayData.js as a shared public holiday and flag day calculation library
- Added CalendarExportPage.qml to the application
- Added the calendar export page to the application menu
- Added public holiday and flag day categories to exported calendar events
- Added descriptions for exported public holiday and flag day events
- Added a monthly flag day list below the monthly public holiday list
- Added a message when the selected month has no flag days
- Added automatic updating of the monthly public holiday and flag day lists when changing months
- Added hiding of the monthly flag day list when flag day display is disabled
- Improved the calculation and display of ISO week numbers
- Removed unnecessary Date.UTC calls from the ISO week number calculation
- Improved calendar event calculations shared between different pages
- Improved handling of the selected day when changing months
- Improved the stability of calendar and flag day settings
- Improved the About page
- Added an AI-SCORE classification to the About page
- Added the AI-SCORE V image and classification information
- Added information about the use of Copilot GPT-5.6 Sol Think during development
- Added expandable AI-SCORE classification descriptions
- Updated the application website link
- Added calendar export files to the CMake build configuration
- Added CalendarExporter sources and headers to the executable target
- Added calendar export QML and JavaScript files to the distribution files
- Added checks for required calendar export source files during CMake configuration
- Updated the CMake configuration for the new source, QML and JavaScript files
- Improved translation support for the calendar export interface
- Improved interface stability and error messages
- The application continues to work entirely offline

